          "The labyrinth has **three semicircular canals** sensing angular acceleration (endolymph deflects the cupula over hair cells) and **two otolith organs - utricle and saccule** - sensing linear acceleration and gravity through calcium carbonate otoconia. [Harrison 22e]",
          "Both vestibular nerves fire tonically at rest; **vertigo arises from asymmetry** - a unilateral lesion makes the brain read the difference as rotation, producing nystagmus with a **slow phase towards and a fast phase away from the damaged side**. [Harrison 22e]",
